From e21d07c27a2235667d1450a003e883b246ed5aa3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 07:42:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Restore dependency-aware mining selection and resource
 accounting

The experimental package accumulator charges already selected ancestors again, which rejects fitting children near block size and sigcheck limits. Its retained ancestor fees also admit unprioritised free descendants and fee deltas leak into grandchildren. The advertised package-priority reset cannot occur for a weighted average bounded by the initial maximum rate.

Restore the retained upstream selection algorithm using the maintained fee-rate index and direct-parent counters. Remove experimental template fields and misleading complexity claims. Restore fee/prioritisation expectations and add a real mainnet-fixture parent/child test with exactly one byte of block capacity spare. The same tests fail five assertions before this repair and pass the miner suite afterward.
---
 src/node/miner.cpp       | 169 +--------------------------------------
 src/node/miner.h         |  67 +---------------
 src/test/miner_tests.cpp |  71 ++++++++++------
 3 files changed, 52 insertions(+), 255 deletions(-)

